{"causes": ["The deposition of his father, Sultan Ibrahim, by Janissaries in 1648, thrust Mehmed IV onto the throne at age six, creating a power vacuum.", "The internal political instability and military defeats that characterized the early 17th-century Ottoman Empire necessitated strong leadership, paving the way for the Köprülü family's rise.", "The ongoing Ottoman-Venetian Wars, particularly the protracted Siege of Candia, created pressure for military and administrative reform during his early reign."], "effects": ["The Köprülü era (1656-1683) temporarily revitalized Ottoman military and administrative power, leading to significant territorial gains in the 1660s and 1670s.", "The catastrophic defeat at the 1683 Siege of Vienna triggered the Great Turkish War and the formation of the Holy League, initiating a century of Ottoman territorial losses in Europe.", "His deposition in 1687 marked a definitive end to the Köprülü-led resurgence, ushering in a period of sustained Ottoman decline and political instability."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "mehmed-iv", "sourceName": "Mehmed IV", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "siege-of-vienna-1683", "targetName": "Siege of Vienna (1683)", "context": "Mehmed IV, as Ottoman Sultan, authorized and oversaw the ambitious, ultimately disastrous, Siege of Vienna in 1683."}, {"sourceSlug": "mehmed-iv", "sourceName": "Mehmed IV", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "edirne-ottoman-empire", "targetName": "Edirne, Ottoman Empire", "context": "Mehmed IV frequently resided in Edirne, transforming it into a secondary capital and conducting much of his hunting and statecraft from there."}, {"sourceSlug": "köprülü-mehmed-pasha", "sourceName": "Köprülü Mehmed Pasha", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "mehmed-iv", "targetName": "Mehmed IV", "context": "As Grand Vizier from 1656, Köprülü Mehmed Pasha exerted significant influence over Mehmed IV, stabilizing the empire and initiating reforms."}, {"sourceSlug": "mehmed-iv", "source